+# TC-v3 client half · AFTER measurement · WHAT RAN, WHAT DID NOT
+
+**Unit** OWNER-RULING-2026-09-03-02, client half · 2026-09-03 · `origin/staging` `78fed3a`
+**`src/` NOT touched this turn**, per instruction.
+
+---
+
+## 1 · v3 IS LIVE — verified, not accepted
+
+`pg_proc` on staging `ztzutckwdhetphwghuzj`, Supabase MCP, SELECT only, **13:08:33.57438 UTC**:
+
+```
+get_top_contributors_v3 -> TABLE(user_id uuid, rank_position integer,
+                                 contributor_score integer, recent_score integer)
+provolatile = s   prosecdef = true   proconfig = {search_path=public}
+anon EXECUTE = true   authenticated EXECUTE = true
+```
+
+**Exactly the frozen §2.2 signature.** `STABLE`, not `VOLATILE`. Grants match v2 and do not exceed
+them. `get_top_contributors_v2` present and unchanged — the rollback is intact. **The interface §3
+precondition is met; the Owner override is retired.**
+
+## 2 · The client half is NOT on staging — so there is no AFTER to measure
+
+`origin/staging` `78fed3a`: `src/hooks/useTopContributors.ts` contains **0** references to
+`get_top_contributors_v3`; `src/pages/Index.tsx` contains **0** references to `recent_score`.
+
+Patch `137882b` has not landed. **Any render taken now measures the OLD card**, and labelling it
+"AFTER" would be false. Not done.
+
+## 3 · The instrument: one blocker fixed, one still standing
+
+| stage | result |
+|---|---|
+| egress preflight (`curl -x $HTTPS_PROXY`) | **200** — passes now; it did not before |
+| Playwright browser binary | **fixed** — the repo pins playwright 1.62.1, which wants `chromium-1234`; this container ships `chromium-1194`. `npx playwright install` is not run here, so the script gained a `TC_V3_CHROME` executablePath override. Unset, behaviour is exactly as delivered |
+| `page.goto` | **`net::ERR_CONNECTION_RESET`**, all four runs |
+
+So the browser now launches and the site is reachable by `curl` through the same proxy, but Chromium's
+connections are reset by it. That is the **fourth** distinct configuration attempted across this
+session. **Stopped rather than continuing, and no geometry is estimated.**
+
+**Still not measured, still owed:** row height, card height, name width, truncation point, at 360 px
+and at real width, REAL and SUBSTITUTED, with screenshots. These need a browser with egress — CI, or
+the Owner's machine. The script is one command and now runs end to end up to the network.
+
+## 4 · ⚠ FINDING — the §3.4 gate cannot discriminate on staging data
+
+`get_top_contributors_v3()` joined to `profiles`, staging, **13:09:11.219771 UTC**:
+
+| rank | name | chars | **recent_score (30d)** | contributor_score (lifetime) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Yuki Tanabe | 11 | **764** | 764 |
+| 2 | Tomas Vogel | 11 | **509** | 509 |
+| 3 | Ari Sen | 7 | **509** | 509 |
+
+**The two fields hold identical values on every row.** The gate asks that the three displayed numbers
+descend — and they do, 764 ≥ 509 ≥ 509. **But they would also descend if the card were still
+rendering `contributor_score`,** because on this data the two are the same number.
+
+**A passing §3.4 run on staging therefore does not prove the fix.** It cannot fail on the defect it
+was written to catch. The interface anticipated half of this — *"non-increasing there, but
+coincidentally"* — but the consequence is stronger than recorded: the check is not merely weak on
+staging, it is **non-discriminating**, exactly as the name-length check was, and for the same reason.
+
+**What does discriminate, and already passed:** the behavioural unit test in
+`src/__tests__/topContributorsV3.home.test.ts` mocks the RPC with production's trio — lifetime
+9,551 / 8,888 / **11,546** against recent 7,055 / 6,978 / 6,823 — and asserts that the ranking number
+descends **while the lifetime number does not**. That assertion fails against the unchanged component
+and passes against the changed one. It is the only check in this unit that can tell the fixed card
+from the broken one.
+
+**Recommendation for the Auditor, not a change made:** close §3.4 against **production** after
+promotion, or against a SUBSTITUTED staging run that injects the production trio — and record that the
+staging run alone is corroborating, not deciding. As it stands, "§3.4 green on staging" would be an
+evidence line that cannot fail.
+
+## 5 · Item 3 re-verified — the skipIf stands
+
+`origin/staging` `78fed3a` `supabase/migrations/` holds only
+`20260725160000_top_contributors_exclude_staff.sql` and `20260811160000_top_contributors_v2.sql`.
+**No v3 migration on origin.** The rollback guard stays `describe.skipIf`, and the filename
+`20260903090000_top_contributors_v3.sql` remains **Auditor-attested, not verified**.
+
+*D2 · Client & Delivery. Read-only against staging. No `src/**` change, no SQL, no `supabase/**`,
+no `docs/gates/**`, no ledger.*
